Changelog: 14-11-2026 03:50:37

Version 4.0.0.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 03:28:53

Breaking. Core's Windows code is removed: a PlayStation 5 running Bazzite never used it. Gone are the modules
portable.py (the handheld window and its widgets), play.py, heat.py, chip.py, power.py, sound_output.py, browse.py
and xbox.py, with images/wallpaper.webp, which only the handheld window used; no app of the suite imported them. In
platform.py: the %LOCALAPPDATA% and %APPDATA% folders (local_data, roaming_config, start_menu), open_path, the touch
keyboard, a window's place on its monitor, the built-in screens, outside_bundle, start_program, the PowerShell
helpers and make_shortcut; launch_in_terminal, show_in_folder and private keep what they did on Linux, and
suite_data and suite_config are ~/.local/share/<suite> and ~/.config/<suite>. In steam.py: the registry, steam.exe
and the wait for a sign-in (hand_over); open_url(url, run) hands the address to xdg-open, as it did here. gone.py
keeps the message box the game managers show (show_dialog) and loses the handheld screen. app.py no longer sets the
.ini format for Windows, and gamepad.py no longer sets SDL_JOYSTICK_RAWINPUT, which SDL reads on Windows alone.
Nothing changes in what the apps do on Bazzite.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 01:28:53

Version 3.2.0.

Changelog: 14-11-2026 01:23:54

Added. app.switch_theme(theme) puts another theme on the running app: the widgets draw with it, the application
takes its palette and style sheet, and the tooltips their border. InfoButton.restyle() and RoundedToolTip.restyle()
write their style sheet again in the theme of the moment; a widget with theme colors in a style sheet of its own
does the same after a switch. For the portal's Theme pill. Nothing changes for an app that never switches.

